# Nova Vitral - Always-on Rules

You are working inside the Nova Vitral design language: modern minimal interfaces with
glassmorphism, dark aurora grounds, 1px hairlines, tight typography, generous whitespace and
restrained scroll-driven motion.

## Specification

Full spec (read only the line ranges you need, never end to end):
`nova-design.md` in the repository root, or
`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pedro21062014/nova-design/main/nova-design.md`

| Need | Read |
|---|---|
| How to deliver, vocabulary | spec 0.4 to 0.8 |
| Tokens (only allowed values) | spec 2 |
| Components | spec 3 |
| Chat / AI interface | spec 4 |
| Complete pages and section order | spec 5 |
| Motion and scroll animation | spec 6 |
| Copy-paste recipes | spec 7 |
| Quality gates and anti-patterns | spec 9 |

Example library (100 examples): `examples/` folder, index at `examples/00-index.md`.

## Hard rules

1. **Tokens only.** No hex, `rgba()`, shadow literal, border radius, blur or duration inside a
   component. Use `var(--token)` or the mapped Tailwind class. Tokens live in `app/globals.css`.
2. **Glass needs a background.** Never `backdrop-filter` over a flat surface; there must be an
   aurora, gradient or image behind it.
3. **Three-layer glass.** Fill + hairline edge (gradient mask) + inner highlight. Nested panels do
   not stack blur; they reduce fill and raise edge contrast.
4. **shadcn/ui is the base.** Do not hand-roll dialogs, menus, popovers, tooltips, selects or
   toasts. Skin them with the vitral classes and map shadcn variables to Nova Vitral tokens.
5. **All states.** default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, empty, error.
6. **Focus rings are never removed.** `outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px` on
   `:focus-visible`.
7. **Motion ladder.** 140ms micro, 240ms standard, 420ms surfaces, 760ms reveals. Nothing above
   900ms. Entrances use `--ease-out`, exits are shorter.
8. **Reveal once.** `once: true`, amount 0.25, margin `0px 0px -12% 0px`, 16px travel (24px for
   large panels), stagger 60 to 80ms clamped so the last sibling starts under 400ms.
9. **Animate `transform` and `opacity` only.** No animating height, top, margin, box-shadow or
   background-position. Height transitions use `grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr`.
10. **Reduced motion.** Every animation has a `prefers-reduced-motion` path that renders the final
    state. Nothing hidden, nothing moving.
11. **Responsive.** Verify 320, 768, 1024, 1440, 1920. No horizontal scroll at any width.
12. **Accessibility.** Semantic HTML, labeled controls, `aria-*` where needed, AA contrast over the
    worst-case backdrop, targets at least 24px (44px on touch).
13. **Performance.** At most six simultaneous `backdrop-filter` elements per viewport; no scroll
    handlers without `{ passive: true }` and rAF; virtualize lists above 60 items; chart and table
    components must not re-render during scroll.
14. **Copy.** Specific, benefit-led, sentence case, no placeholders, no "Lorem ipsum", no invented
    attribution. UI text in the project language; code and identifiers in English.
15. **No emojis** in production UI, code comments or commit messages.

## Conventions

- Files `kebab-case.tsx`, named exports, one component per file, props typed and exported.
- Class merging with `cn()` (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`); variants with `cva`.
- Client components only where interactivity exists; prefer server components.
- Hooks in `lib/hooks`, motion helpers in `components/motion`, primitives in `components/ui`.
- Nothing outside the token layer may define colors, shadows or timings.

## Motion tokens

```ts
export const t = {
  micro: { duration: 0.14, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  base: { duration: 0.24, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  surface: { duration: 0.42, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  reveal: { duration: 0.76, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] },
  spring: { type: "spring", stiffness: 260, damping: 26, mass: 0.9 },
} as const;
```

## Anti-patterns that must be rejected

Purple gradients on every surface; glass over flat backgrounds; emoji icons; three pulsing badges in
one viewport; reveal animations that replay on scroll up; cards scaling to 1.05 on hover; "Feature
one" copy; "John Doe, CEO" testimonials; toasts for copying; spinners instead of streaming in chat;
auto-approving agent actions that write or spend; disabling focus outlines.

## Before finishing any change

1. Grep your own diff for hex colors and raw durations outside the tokens file.
2. Confirm hover, focus, disabled and loading states for each new interactive element.
3. Confirm the reduced-motion path.
4. Confirm 320px layout with no horizontal scroll.
5. State in three bullets: built, omitted, next step.
